                    <th>Interpretation</th>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Maximum Drawdown</td>
                    <td class="negative">{kpis['max_drawdown']:.1f}%</td>
                    <td>Largest peak-to-trough decline in 26 years</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                    <td>Annualized Volatility</td>
                    <td>{kpis['annualized_volatility']:.1f}%</td>
                    <td>Typical range for consumer discretionary</td>
                </tr>
            </table>
        </div>

        <!-- Volume Analysis -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Trading Volume Patterns</h2>
            <p>Average daily trading volume of {format_volume(kpis['avg_daily_volume'])} shares indicates strong liquidity. Volume spikes often correlate with significant price events:</p>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['volume']}" alt="Nike Volume Analysis">
            </div>

            <h3>Volume Periods of Interest</h3>
            <div class="insight-box">
                <p><strong>February 2000 (Ultra-High Volume):</strong> Volume exceeded 65M shares on Feb 8-9, 2000. This coincided with the sharpest price decline during the dot-com bust, indicating panic selling and high volatility.</p>
                <p><strong>2008–2009 Crisis:</strong> Elevated volume throughout the financial crisis as investors reassessed positions amid market uncertainty.</p>
                <p><strong>2020 COVID Crash:</strong> Significant volume spikes in March 2020 during the pandemic-induced selloff, followed by equally dramatic recovery volumes.</p>
                <p><strong>Post-Pandemic Trading:</strong> Volume normalized but remained elevated compared to pre-2020 levels, reflecting increased retail investor participation.</p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Annual Performance -->
        <div class="section">
            <h2>Annual and Decade-Level Performance Breakdown</h2>

            <div class="chart-container">
                <img src="data:image/png;base64,{charts['annual_returns']}" alt="Nike Annual Returns">
            </div>

            <h3>Best and Worst Performing Years</h3>
            <div class="two-col">
                <div>
                    <h4 style="color: #276749;">Top 5 Best Years</h4>
                    <table class="data-table">
                        <tr><th>Year</th><th>Return</th></tr>
"""

