""".format(1000 * (1 + kpis['cumulative_return']/100), kpis['end_date'].strftime('%B %Y'), (1 + kpis['cumulative_return']/100))

    html += f"""                <li><strong>CAGR of {kpis['cagr']:.2f}%:</strong> Nike's compound annual growth rate of {kpis['cagr']:.2f}% has been substantial, reflecting consistent execution of its business strategy over decades.</li>
                <li><strong>Volatility is Priced In:</strong> With {kpis['annualized_volatility']:.1f}% annualized volatility, Nike is a moderately volatile large-cap stock. Risk-tolerant investors comfortable with drawdowns have been rewarded with superior long-term returns.</li>
                <li><strong>Maximum Drawdown of {kpis['max_drawdown']:.1f}%:</strong> While painful in absolute terms, Nike's maximum drawdown of {kpis['max_drawdown']:.1f}% was relatively contained compared to many growth stocks, suggesting some defensive characteristics of the brand.</li>
                <li><strong>Volume as a Signal:</strong> Unusual volume spikes during the dot-com bust, 2008 crisis, and COVID crash presented both risks and opportunities. Investors who maintained conviction during these periods were rewarded.</li>
                <li><strong>Decade Consistency:</strong> Nike delivered positive returns in most decades, with particularly strong performance in the 2000s and 2010s. The 2020s show continued relevance though with increased volatility.</li>
                <li><strong>Direct-to-Consumer Transformation:</strong> The shift toward digital channels and owned retail has supported margins and customer relationships, potentially making the business more resilient in competitive零售 environments.</li>
            </ul>
